ne one  with the dominant super villain gene  but morocco is still haunted by the man  he was 20 years ago and in this case  it's literal  the time displaced morocc from the past  finds his present self and reminds him  of what he wanted to be  past mordock shows his older self all of  the futures that could occur  deaths at the hands of every avenger  toilet heart attacks and presciently  that one potential outcome that sees  modoc become the ruler of a utopian  unified earth  you're a super villain you hate the  world  no i don't i just want to change it it's  a strange setup that calls back to dr  strange's infinity war scenario of a one  chance in 14 million for victory with  one dark  difference in infinity war tony stark  has come to terms with how much of  himself he'll sacrifice while modoc can  succeed only if he sacrifices others  specifically the family that he worked  so hard to deserve  the key word there the one that cemented  the family's doom  is worked it's unavoidable that marvel's  modoc is going to be compared to adult  swims rick and morty as they both have  science fiction elements pop culture  references and self-serving cartoon  geniuses so it's fitting that a line  from rick and morty can sum up the  general theme of modoc season one  the thing about repairing maintaining  and cleaning is  it's not an adventure there's no way to  do it so wrong you might die  it's just work that's a conundrum at the  center of modoc take the exciting  destructive dramatic path or keep  working at the day-to-day aspects of  life  nco kill iron man or clean your  apartment conundrum  one option means that modok's mother was  right and he's a very special boy  the other means doing the work and if  his younger self is to be believed  never becoming what he dreamed he would  be melissa's earlier attempts to teach  her old man how to take the subtle  effective route to echo through his  decision  and modoc stands at the same proverbial  fork in the road as every 